{
  "id": "028",
  "title": "Return to Blackwell",
  "subtitle": "\"Two years after my husband died, I moved to the Vermont house he left me. My husband's oldest friend was still there, still taking care of it, still waiting.\"",
  "penName": "Cece Voss",
  "genre": "secondChance",
  "hook": "My husband David died of a sudden cardiac event in our Brooklyn apartment at thirty-six. He left me his grandmother's lake house in Blackwell, Vermont — a place I had visited twice and not loved. Two years later I packed two bags and drove. Nate Hart opened the door. He was David's oldest friend, had been the best man at our wedding, had mowed this yard for the last decade. He said *Cece* and handed me a set of keys and a key lime pie. His hands shook. His hands had never shaken before. I understood.",
